Subject: [PATCH] Report tiled positions and transfer switcher keyboard focus

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Apply after patches 0001 through 0013 on niri v26.04. Upstream IPC reports
tile_pos_in_workspace_view for floating windows only (patch 0013 adds an inset
fullscreen tile), so a shell cannot tell where a tiled window is on screen and
cannot cut its picture out of a screen capture (the Alt+Tab window switcher).
WindowLayout gains emaki_tile_pos_in_view: the tile's position in the view of
its workspace for every scrolling tile, at the view's target scroll position
and rounded to physical pixels as rendered, so it equals the drawn position
once the view rests and a scroll animation changes it once, not every frame.
tile_pos_in_workspace_view keeps its meaning. The field is optional and
omitted when absent, so upstream clients read the JSON unchanged. The additive
emaki_capture_safe field tells crop consumers whether settled coordinates are
usable: false during output transitions (including gestures), overview or an
interactive move. Consumers must treat an absent flag as unsafe. Safety changes
use the existing layout event channel, without per-frame coordinate events.

Explicit window focus actions also retire on-demand layer focus and update the
seat before the next input callback. The shell keeps its overlay on-demand until
the chosen window is confirmed. Tests record wl_keyboard delivery in both arrival
orders, including the unsupported early-release gap, for explicit and previous
window actions, and preserve exclusive-layer and missing-target behavior.

